\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 The }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\insrsid5906206\charrsid5906206 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Weight Tuner}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid5906206\charrsid5906206 
\hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506  tab lets you drag each factor's weight and see the mentor rankings re-sort in real time. The }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\insrsid5906206\charrsid5906206 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 
Algorithm Pipeline}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid5906206\charrsid5906206 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506  tab shows each phase with its complexity class. A few design notes worth highlighting:
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\insrsid5906206\charrsid5906206 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 On the bitmap availability check}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid5906206\charrsid5906206 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506  
\hich\f31506 \emdash \loch\f31506  encoding a mentor's weekly schedule as a 168-bit integer (one bit per hour of the week) means computing overlap between learner and mentor becomes a single BitSet AND + popcount \hich\f31506 \emdash \loch\f31506 
 effectively O(1) regardless of how complex the schedules are. This is fa\hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 r cheaper than comparing datetime ranges.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\insrsid5906206\charrsid5906206 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 On the heap vs full sort}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid5906206\charrsid5906206 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506  \hich\f31506 
\emdash \loch\f31506 \hich\f31506  if you sorted all n mentors to get Top-K, you'd pay O(n log n). The min-heap approach pays O(n log k) instead, which for k=10 and n=10,000 cuts the work by roughly 3\'d7.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\insrsid5906206\charrsid5906206 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 On reputation decoupling}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid5906206\charrsid5906206 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506  \hich\f31506 
\emdash \loch\f31506 \hich\f31506  the PageRank pass runs nightly as a batch job over the review graph (O(V+E) per iteration \'d7\loch\f31506  ~20 iterations). At query time the result is already stored on the MentorNode
\hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 , so the matching function reads it in O(1). This keeps the real-time path fast while still reflecting complex trust relationships.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 For the Laravel implementation, the inverted index maps naturally to a PostgreSQL GIN index on a skill_tags array column, and the heap can live in PHP's SplPriorityQueue.
